{title: Faith of Our Fathers}
{artist: Frederick W. Faber / Henri F. Hemy}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening, Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}
{score: faith-of-our-fathers.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Faith of our [C]fathers! [G]living [D]still
In [Em]spite of [C]dungeon, [G]fire and [D]sword
O [G]how our [C]hearts beat [G]high with [D]joy
When[Em]e'er we [C]hear that [G]glorious [D]word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Faith of our [C]fathers, [G]holy [D]faith
We will be [Em]true to [C]thee till [G]death
[G]Faith of our [C]fathers, [G]holy [D]faith
We will be [Em]true to [C]thee till [G]death
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Our fathers, [C]chained in [G]prisons [D]dark
Were [Em]still in [C]heart and [G]conscience [D]free
How [G]sweet would [C]be their [G]children's [D]fate
If [Em]they, like [C]them, could [G]die for [D]thee
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Faith of our [C]fathers! [G]we will [D]love
Both [Em]friend and [C]foe in [G]all our [D]strife
And [G]preach thee, [C]too, as [G]love knows [D]how
By [Em]kindly [C]words and [G]virtuous [D]life
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
